# Vault .gitattributes template (T-02-32).
#
# Installed as the private data repo's own `.gitattributes` (Plan 07, with
# the user's OK). Named without a leading dot here so it never applies
# inside this (public) repo's own working copy.

# LF everywhere, so the job (Linux runner) and a developer's local clone
# never disagree on line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Raw fetched responses stay byte-exact: RawCache's manifest sha256 values
# are computed against the exact bytes on disk, so these must never be
# normalized (CRLF/LF, encoding, or otherwise).
raw/** -text

# Append-only ledgers: the job (Sunday/Wednesday) and a local run can each
# append a new line to the same JSONL file between one push and the next.
# merge=union keeps both sides' lines on a rebase conflict instead of
# leaving conflict markers, so job and local commits rebase cleanly.
ledger/*.jsonl merge=union
